docs {
  # LEA client endpoint access (ONEROSTER-59)

  Uses the LEA token from the `oauth` folder (`lea-odsApiToken`, which holds the
  non-demographics `roster.readonly` and `roster-core.readonly` scopes) to call
  `academicSessions`, `orgs`, `courses` and `classes`, and checks that each:

  - returns HTTP 200
  - returns exactly the number of records in the LEA baseline for the data set

  The baselines come from the `LEA_*_TOTAL` variables in the E2E env file for the
  data standard, engine and install type under test (`environments/*.env`), exposed
  to Bruno as `lea*Total`. Each request asks for `maxPageSize` records so a single
  response holds the whole view; the test fails if a baseline exceeds that ceiling.
}
